.Dd March 2, 2026
.Dt ELF_RISCV_ATTRIBUTE_TAG_AT 3
.Os Substrate
.Sh NAME
.Nm elf_riscv_attribute_tag_at
.Nd return a parsed RISC-V attribute tag by index
.Sh LIBRARY
.Lb libelfobj
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In elfobj.h
.Ft uint32_t
.Fn elf_riscv_attribute_tag_at "const elfobj_t *obj" "size_t index"
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Fn elf_riscv_attribute_tag_at
function parses
.Pa .riscv.attributes
from
.Fa obj
and returns the tag number for the entry at
.Fa index .
.Pp
Use
.Xr elf_riscv_attribute_count 3
first to determine the valid index range.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
The
.Fn elf_riscv_attribute_tag_at
function returns the tag value for the requested entry.
It returns 0 if
.Fa obj
is
.Dv NULL ,
if
.Fa index
is out of range,
or if parsing fails.
.Sh CAVEATS
A returned value of 0 can indicate failure or an actual attribute tag value of 0.
Callers that need strict disambiguation should validate bounds with
.Xr elf_riscv_attribute_count 3
before indexing.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr elf_riscv_attribute_count 3 ,
.Xr elf_riscv_attribute_value_at 3 ,
.Xr elfobj 3
